{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf5k9jHM2Ry2bgMfRqPCG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a complete understanding of the repository structure and conventions. Let me move to the design phase.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** - Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to ErrorCode enum. This error code represents an attempt to confirm a shipment in an invalid state (specifically CANCELLED).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** - Add a new `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` method that:\n   - Retrieves the shipment by ID (throws ResourceNotFoundException if not found)\n   - Checks if the shipment status is CANCELLED (throws ConflictException if so)\n   - Updates the shipment to CONFIRMED status (save a new copy with CONFIRMED status)\n   - Returns the updated shipment with HTTP 200 OK\n   - The method is idempotent: if the shipment is already CONFIRMED, it simply returns it unchanged\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add four test methods:\n   - `confirms a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED status` - happy path\n   - `confirm is idempotent for already CONFIRMED shipments` - confirms CONFIRMED shipment returns same shipment without changes\n   - `rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment with 409` - throws ConflictException with proper error code\n   - `rejects confirming a non-existent shipment with 404` - throws ResourceNotFoundException\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\nI considered adding a service layer between controller and repository, but rejected it because:\n- The existing codebase uses controller-to-repository pattern (see ShipmentController using repository directly)\n- The ticket specifically says \"do not modify files outside the shipment feature\" except tests\n- A service layer would add unnecessary complexity for this simple state transition\n- The existing shipment controller already handles business logic directly\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n*Happy path (CREATED → CONFIRMED):*\n- Request: POST /shipments/S-1/confirm (empty body or ignored)\n- Controller retrieves shipment by ID from repository\n- Status is CREATED, so proceed\n- Create new Shipment object with status=CONFIRMED\n- Save to repository\n- Return 200 OK with updated Shipment object\n\n*Idempotent case (already CONFIRMED):*\n- Request: POST /shipments/S-1/confirm\n- Controller retrieves shipment by ID\n- Status is CONFIRMED, skip update (or update is idempotent)\n- Return 200 OK with Shipment object\n\n*Invalid state case (CANCELLED):*\n- Request: POST /shipments/S-1/confirm\n- Controller retrieves shipment by ID\n- Status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE, message)\n- GlobalExceptionHandler catches it, returns 409 with ApiError envelope\n\n*Not found case:*\n- Request: POST /shipments/missing/confirm\n- Controller calls findById, gets null\n- Throw ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, message)\n- GlobalExceptionHandler catches it, returns 404 with ApiError envelope\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. Test \"confirms a CREATED shipment\" - Create S-1, call confirm, verify status changed to CONFIRMED\n2. Test \"confirm is idempotent\" - Create S-1, confirm once, confirm again, verify still CONFIRMED and no error\n3. Test \"reject CANCELLED\" - Create S-1, manually update to CANCELLED via repository.save(), call confirm, expect 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE code\n4. Test \"reject non-existent\" - Call confirm on S-missing, expect 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nLet me start by adding the error code to the ErrorCode enum:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":419,"cache_read_input_tokens":18294,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":419},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d502f22d-0673-4f78-82a4-de8e2cf8d471","uuid":"48bc05bb-1713-4c4c-bbd0-757a0c24d908","timestamp":"2026-09-15T19:03:54.568Z","request_id":"req_011Cf5k9j2DDbQ758Spds7yB"}
